& [Purpose] is compile what must be covered before designing how to cover it
  + preserve exact semantic boundaries between schema grammar domain fields typed bindings ingress residuals and resource profiles
  + produce inspectable obligation identities and relations
  + expose divergence candidates without deciding results

& [AuthorityState] is formation_only
  + zero requirements are implemented or verified
  + no executable compiler output catalogue case fixture or signature exists

& [InputIdentity] is conjunctive
  + exact I02 bundle and five root document digests
  + exact source artifacts containing the selected Rust bindings and custom types
  + exact I03B ingress profile I03C residual registry I03D reader profile and I03E report profile
  + future activation binds the exact post-I03D Cargo lock code snapshot and compiler profile
  + any mismatch prevents obligation formation output

& [SchemaGrammarTraversal] is Draft 2020-12 aware
  + begin at one admitted root SchemaNode
  + traverse named child schemas under dollar defs properties patternProperties and dependentSchemas
  + traverse child arrays under allOf anyOf oneOf and prefixItems
  + traverse child schemas under items contains propertyNames not if then else and schema-valued additional or unevaluated keywords
  + record boolean schemas explicitly
  + never interpret a domain name inside a named-child map as a keyword

& [SchemaPointer] uses canonical JSON Pointer
  + UTF-8 member names are escaped with tilde-zero and tilde-one only
  + array positions use canonical base-10 index without leading zero
  + pointer length and segment counts obey I03D limits
  + duplicate decoded member names are impossible after admitted I03B ingress

& [SchemaRuleSite] is physical identity
  + root kind document digest pointer keyword role raw operand digest normalized operand digest and optional reference target
  + two sites remain distinct even when their normalized definitions match
  + base_response and preparation_response sites always remain distinct

& [RuleRoles] are closed
  + assertion can affect instance acceptance under the fixed validator profile
  + applicator selects or combines child schemas
  + annotation records meaning without instance rejection in the fixed profile
  + identity binds dialect document or anchor identity
  + container owns child schemas but creates no instance assertion by itself
  + reference links one physical site to an in-document target

& [OperandNormalization] is keyword-specific and lossless
  + retain raw canonical JSON digest for every site
  + required and type arrays normalize as unique lexical sets after meta validity
  + enum values normalize as unique canonical JSON values
  + numeric operands retain exact token and mathematical relation
  + branch sites retain physical child index while canonical unordered applicator definitions may sort child definition digests
  + prefixItems retains order
  + no normalization may change a physical site or error location

& [CanonicalRuleDefinition] supports reuse without authority merge
  + bind keyword role normalized operand and normalized child shape
  + equivalent definitions may share an ObligationTemplate
  + each root site still emits its own RootRuleObligation and later requires explicit root execution evidence

& [ReferenceGraph] is non-expanding
  + every dollar ref site emits one ReferenceClosureEdge
  + only a valid resolved local pointer or anchor target is admitted
  + target site identities are referenced rather than cloned beneath every edge
  + cycles are recorded through edges and bounded traversal state rather than native recursion
  + unresolved external malformed escaping dynamic or over-limit targets are upstream faults

& [AssertionObligationProjection] is deterministic
  + type emits admitted-type positive and bounded wrong-type negative templates
  + each required member emits presence and omission obligations
  + each enum value emits positive relation and each enum site emits one outside-value negative relation
  + const emits exact and changed-value relations
  + minimum emits below at and above when representable
  + minLength maxLength and pattern emit relevant boundary and mismatch relations
  + uniqueItems true emits unique positive and duplicate negative relations
  + additionalProperties false emits declared-property positive and unknown-property negative relations
  + schema-valued additionalProperties emits matching and nonmatching map-value relations

& [ApplicatorObligationProjection] is deterministic
  + anyOf emits each reachable-branch positive and no-branch negative relations
  + oneOf emits each exactly-one branch positive no-branch negative and multi-branch ambiguity negative relations where constructible
  + branch constructibility is a later case-planning status and absence remains visible
  + `$ref` emits reference-edge closure separately from target assertions

& [AnnotationProjection] is non-assertive
  + format sites remain annotation obligations because I03D validates formats false and ignores unknown formats
  + int64 uint32 and uint64 annotations do not synthesize schema maxima
  + dollar schema dollar id title and exact dialect become configuration or identity observations

& [ObservedAuditBaseline] is evidence to replay not hard-coded output authority
  + five roots contain 344 root-qualified definitions 2318 property members 77 pattern-property members 2271 required members and 818 enum values
  + grammar-aware sites include type 1667 const 140 minimum-zero 265 uniqueItems 231 required 372 additionalProperties 493 items 269 oneOf 14 anyOf 83 dollar-ref 1599 and format 280
  + additionalProperties divides into 449 false and 44 schema-valued
  + oneOf has 140 physical branches and anyOf 166
  + format divides into int64 15 uint32 5 and uint64 260
  + grammar-aware maximum site count is zero
  + compiler replay must reproduce or explicitly fault against these exact-source observations

& [TypedSourceBinding] is explicit rather than inferred from schema alone
  + bind Rust type source artifact digest source locator serde attributes direction field path and destination representation
  + input operations are PrepareRequest PreparedRunRequest and VerifyRequest exact-byte deserialization
  + output operations are actual ProcedureToolResponse serialization under base and preparation intended uses
  + presence modes are required_nonnull required_nullable optional_nonnull optional_nullable skipped_when_none and not_applicable

& [DirectionRules] prevent false commonality
  + input byte mutations can be compared only when both schema and typed deserializer apply
  + response typed evidence must originate from a constructible actual value
  + a schema-negative output mutation not emitted by any actual value is schema_only
  + shared response type never collapses two root intended uses

& [DivergenceCandidateProjection] is non-verdict evidence
  + uniqueItems versus duplicate-collapsing set deserialization candidate
  + ignored numeric format versus Rust representation range candidate
  + schema required-nullable versus serde missing Option candidate
  + skip-on-none versus required-output presence candidate
  + actual I03D observation is required before any candidate becomes agreement disagreement or finding

& [IngressObligations] are independent
  + valid UTF-8 one complete value trailing whitespace decoded duplicate identity numeric token and structural limits
  + below at above for exact byte depth member item scalar name and work limits
  + ingress refusal blocks later readers and therefore has no CommonSyntaxClaim

& [ResidualObligations] preserve all I03C records
  + root applicability type enforcement disposition evaluation policy source binding and proof identity
  + safe_pure produces later complete-fixture evaluation targets
  + observational_only produces evidence-presence and non-overclaim targets
  + prohibited_authority produces non-invocation and zero-effect targets
  + unimplemented or partial disposition remains a visible non-passing condition

& [ResourceObligations] are not invented schema keywords
  + I03B I03D and I03E finite profiles may emit below-at-above resource boundaries
  + absent maxItems maxProperties or numeric maximum in schema cannot be represented as schema assertions
  + every source profile remains identified in the obligation

& [ObligationIdentity] is stable
  + domain-separated digest of profile root direction kind source identity canonical rule polarity boundary applicability mandatory severity and rationale digest
  + changing any normative field creates a successor identity
  + relation ids bind source target kind and rationale

& [CompilerOutput] is non-executing
  + input ledger schema sites canonical definitions reference edges typed sites ingress sites residual sites obligations relations accounts and output digest
  + contains no case fixture expectation reader observation semantic result agreement finding coverage satisfaction pass signature or activation
  + normative order is complete and lexical

& [DeterminismProof] after future activation is dual reconstruction
  + compiler output A from exact bound inputs
  + independently reconstructed output B using the same specification and separate traversal state
  + exact canonical byte and digest equality
  + accounts recomputed from records rather than trusted

& [Limits] are finite
  + all parent schema document reference depth path residual and report limits apply
  + site obligation relation template and diagnostic maxima must be fixed in a later activation source before allocation
  + every counter product offset recursion forecast and allocation uses checked arithmetic

& [FutureSourceTouch] remains inside the I03E activation inventory
  + no separate Cargo dependency
  + implementation location is conformance_report.rs or a separately source-preserved obligation_compiler.rs selected before signature
  + focused test and compile-time inventory paths are enumerated exactly
  + no runtime file read or write

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + source SJS canonical exploded requirements justification plan review inactive lock proof narrative and evidence metadata only
  - never: Rust compiler catalogue case fixture parser validator reader semantic invocation compatibility admission provider model service persistence network effect production hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [Disposition] is canonical_formation_complete_implementation_refused
